CONVERSATION:
any ideas how to redirect any connections from 8080 to 80 port ?
iptables -t nat -A PREROUTING -p tcp -d ip --dport 8080 -j DNAT --to-destination ip:22 don't work
hello everyone
I'm migrating to a new server and I'm using iptables to make the transition as smooth as possible - to bridge the time it takes for all DNS servers to update.
scpecifically I'm telling the old server to redirect all traffic to the new server.
so, to move the e-mail service I'd do:
iptables -t nat -A PREROUTING -s 0.0.0.0/0 -d  IP1  -p tcp --dport 25 -j DNAT --to IP2
iptables -t nat -A POSTROUTING -s 0.0.0.0/0 -d IP2  -p tcp --dport 25  -j SNAT --to IP1
